{"title": "Sectional Mock #85 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>If m and n are whole numbers such that m<sup>n</sup> = 121, then the value of (m  -  1)<sup>n + 1</sup> is</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; m &#2324;&#2352; n &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; m<sup>n</sup> = 121 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (m - 1) n + 1 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;:__</p>", "options_en": ["1", "10", "121", "1000"], "options_hi": ["1", "10", "121", "1000"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>We know that,</p><p>11<sup>2</sup> = 121</p><p>Putting m = 11 and n = 2, we get</p><p>(m  -  1)<sup>n + 1</sup> = (11  -  1)<sup>2 + 1</sup> = 10<sup>3</sup> = 1000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that,</p><p>11<sup>2</sup> = 121</p><p>Putting m = 11 and n = 2, we get</p><p>(m  -  1)<sup>n + 1</sup> = (11  -  1)<sup>2 + 1</sup> = 10<sup>3</sup> = 1000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Find the value of: (sec &theta; + cosec &theta; -&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p>(sec &#952; + cosec &#952; -1/sin &#952; cos &#952; ) (1 + sin &#952; + cos &#952;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "-1", "-2", "1"], "options_hi": ["2", "-1", "-2", "1"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=316 height=316 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11734/image015.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=316 height=316 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11734/image015.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>A man drives his car for 24 km at a speed of 48 km/h, and for the next 1.5 hours he drives at a speed of 80 km/h. Find his average speed (in km/h) for the entire journey.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; 24 km &#2340;&#2325; 48 km/h &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; 1.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2340;&#2325; &#2357;&#2361; 80 km/h &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; (km/h &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["64", "72", "68", "75"], "options_hi": ["64", "72", "68", "75"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total distance covered = 24 + 1.5 * 80 = 144 km</p><p>Total time = 24/48 + 1.5 = 2 hours</p><p>Average speed = Total distance/Total time = 144/2</p><p>= 72 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total distance covered = 24 + 1.5 * 80 = 144 km</p><p>Total time = 24/48 + 1.5 = 2 hours</p><p>Average speed = Total distance/Total time = 144/2</p><p>= 72 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;The value of&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2&radic;5", "q_hi": "<p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">2&radic;5", "options_en": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "options_hi": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Rationalize first term of the expression:</p><p><img width=236 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image022.gif\"></p><p>Rationalize second term of the expression:</p><p><img width=324 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image023.gif\"></p><p>The expression is:</p><p><img width=320 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image024.gif\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Rationalize first term of the expression:</p><p><img width=236 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image022.gif\"></p><p>Rationalize second term of the expression:</p><p><img width=324 height=49 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image023.gif\"></p><p>The expression is:</p><p><img width=320 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image024.gif\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three persons start a", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; 3: 8: 5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2305;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;, &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2352;&#2369;.600 &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.2400", "Rs.5400", "Rs.4000", "Rs.4800"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.2400", "&#2352;&#2369;.5400", "&#2352;&#2369;.4000", "&#2352;&#2369;.4800"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Capital ratio = 3: 8: 5</p><p>Given that,</p><p>5 - 3 units = Rs.600</p><p>2 units = 600</p><p>1 unit = Rs.300</p><p>16 units = Rs.4800</p><p>SO, total profit = Rs.4800</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Capital ratio = 3: 8: 5</p><p>Given that,</p><p>5 - 3 units = Rs.600</p><p>2 units = 600</p><p>1 unit = Rs.300</p><p>16 units = Rs.4800</p><p>SO, total profit = Rs.4800</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The bar graph given below shows the number of male and female candidates appeared in an exam from five states and the line graph given below shows the number of male and female candidates qualified in the exam from five states.</p><p><img width=506 height=336 id=\"Chart 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image022.png\"></p><p><img width=524 height=336 id=\"Chart 23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image023.png\"></p><p>The number of male candidates in UP who didn't qualify the exam is what percentage of the number of female candidates in HP who didn't qualify the exam? (rounded off to one decimal)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2311;&#2344; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=506 height=336 id=\"Chart 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image022.png\"></p><p><img width=524 height=336 id=\"Chart 23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image023.png\"></p><p>&#2351;&#2370;&#2346;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2319;&#2330;&#2346;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;)</p>", "options_en": ["95.2%", "87.8%", "92.6%", "82.4%"], "options_hi": ["95.2%", "87.8%", "92.6%", "82.4%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Number of male candidates in UP who didn't qualify the exam = 320  -  120 = 200</p><p>Number of female candidates in HP who didn't qualify the exam = 250  -  40 = 210</p><p>Required percentage = (200/210)*100 = 95.2%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of male candidates in UP who didn't qualify the exam = 320  -  120 = 200</p><p>Number of female candidates in HP who didn't qualify the exam = 250  -  40 = 210</p><p>Required percentage = (200/210)*100 = 95.2%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>70ml of 60% concentration of acid X solution is added to 50 ml of 64% concentration of acid X solution. What is the concentration of acid X in the new solution?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>60% &#2360;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; X &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; 70 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; 64% &#2360;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; X &#2325;&#2375; &#2328;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; 50 &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2368;&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2351;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; X &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["61.99%", "61.66%", "61.33%", "61.22%"], "options_hi": ["61.99%", "61.66%", "61.33%", "61.22%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Concentration of acid X in 70 ml of solution = 70 * 60/100 = 42 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in 50 ml of solution = 50 * 64/100 = 32 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in new solution = 42 + 32 = 74 ml</p><p>Required percentage = (74/120) * 100 = 185/3 = 61. 66%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Concentration of acid X in 70 ml of solution = 70 * 60/100 = 42 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in 50 ml of solution = 50 * 64/100 = 32 ml</p><p>Concentration of acid X in new solution = 42 + 32 = 74 ml</p><p>Required percentage = (74/120) * 100 = 185/3 = 61. 66%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If it is given that for two right angled triangles ABC and DFE, &#8736;A = 25&deg;, &#8736;E = 25&deg;, &#8736;B = &#8736;F = 90&deg; and AC = ED, then which one of the following is TRUE?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2351;&#2361; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2324;&#2352; DFE &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#8736;A = 25&deg;, &#8736;E = 25&deg;, &#8736;B = &#8736;F = 90&deg; &#2324;&#2352; AC = ED &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346; <b>&#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; </b>&#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;FED", "&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;DFE", "&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;EFD", "&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;DEF"], "options_hi": ["&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;FED", "&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;DFE", "&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;EFD", "&#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;DEF"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=275 height=177 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22005/image034.png\"></p><p><b>Given:</b></p><p>&#8736;A = &#8736;E = 25&deg;</p><p>&#8736;B = &#8736;F = 90&deg;</p><p>AC = ED</p><p>Which means &#916;ABC and &#916;EFD will be congruent triangles.</p><p>So, &#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;EFD</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=275 height=177 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22005/image034.png\"></p><p><b>Given:</b></p><p>&#8736;A = &#8736;E = 25&deg;</p><p>&#8736;B = &#8736;F = 90&deg;</p><p>AC = ED</p><p>Which means &#916;ABC and &#916;EFD will be congruent triangles.</p><p>So, &#916;ABC &#8773; &#916;EFD</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A certain sum amounts to &#8377;32210.2 in 15 months at the rate of 40% per annum compounded quarterly. Find the value of sum.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 40% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 15 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;32210.2 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;24000", "&#8377;13600", "&#8377;20000", "&#8377;25200"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;24000", "&#8377;13600", "&#8377;20000", "&#8377;25200"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>A = &#8377;32210.2, n = 15/3 = 5, R = 40/4 = 10%</p><p>32210.2 = P * (1 + 10/100)<sup>5</sup></p><p>32210.2 = P * (11/10)<sup>5</sup></p><p>P = 0.2 * 100000</p><p>P = &#8377;20000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A = &#8377;32210.2, n = 15/3 = 5, R = 40/4 = 10%</p><p>32210.2 = P * (1 + 10/100)<sup>5</sup></p><p>32210.2 = P * (11/10)<sup>5</sup></p><p>P = 0.2 * 100000</p><p>P = &#8377;20000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many spherical lead shots each of diameter 8.4 cm can be obtained from a rectangular solid of lead with dimension 88 cm, 63 cm, 42 cm (take &#960; = 22/7)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366; 88 cm, 63 cm, 42 cm (&#960; = 22/7 &#2354;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;) &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2375;/&#2354;&#2375;&#2337; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2360;&#2375; 8.4 cm &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2375;&#2337; &#2358;&#2377;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["920", "750", "650", "860"], "options_hi": ["920", "750", "650", "860"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Diameter of spherical lead shots = 8.4 cm</p><p>Radius of spherical lead shots = 8.4/2 = 4.2 cm</p><p>Since volume of the object will remain constant.</p><p>Let 'n' number of lead balls can be obtained.</p><p>So, Volume of 'n' spherical balls = Volume of rectangular solid</p><p><img width=88 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=176 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=201 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image069.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image070.png\"></p><p>n = 750</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Diameter of spherical lead shots = 8.4 cm</p><p>Radius of spherical lead shots = 8.4/2 = 4.2 cm</p><p>Since volume of the object will remain constant.</p><p>Let 'n' number of lead balls can be obtained.</p><p>So, Volume of 'n' spherical balls = Volume of rectangular solid</p><p><img width=88 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=176 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=201 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=145 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image069.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21853/image070.png\"></p><p>n = 750</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A vessel contains 40 litres of acid. 5 litres of acid is taken out of the vessel and replaced by the same quantity of water. Next 5 litres of the mixture are withdrawn, and again the vessel is filled with the same quantity of water. Find the ratio of acid left in the vessel with the quantity of acid initially in the vessel</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 5 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2346;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; 5 &#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2354; &#2349;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["9:16", "49:64", "16:25", "25:51"], "options_hi": ["9:16", "49:64", "16:25", "25:51"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Remaining acid in the vessel = 40(1-5/40)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(1-1/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(7/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 30.625 litres</p><p>Hence required ratio is 30.625:40 = 49:64</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Remaining acid in the vessel = 40(1-5/40)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(1-1/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 40(7/8)<sup>2 </sup>= 30.625 litres</p><p>Hence required ratio is 30.625:40 = 49:64</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A certain sum amounts to Rs.470.4 in 2 years and to Rs.499.8 in 3 years on compound annually. How much will be the simple interest (in Rs.) on Rs.24000 at the same rate for 4 years?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.470.4 &#2324;&#2352; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.499.8 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2352;&#2369;.24000 &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; 4 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; (&#2352;&#2369;. &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.6000", "Rs.7500", "Rs.4800", "Rs.5400"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.6000", "&#2352;&#2369;.7500", "&#2352;&#2369;.4800", "&#2352;&#2369;.5400"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the sum is Rs. P.</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>470.4 = P * (1 + r/100)<sup>2</sup>...(1)</p><p>And</p><p>499.8 = P * (1 + /100)<sup>3</sup>...(2)</p><p>From equation (1) and (2),</p><p>470.4/499.8 = 1/(1 + r/100)</p><p>112/119 = 1/(1 + r/100)</p><p>112 + 112r/100 = 119</p><p>r = 700/112 = 6.25%</p><p>Now,</p><p>SI = 24000 * 6.25 * 4/100</p><p>SI = 240 * 25</p><p>SI = Rs.6000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the sum is Rs. P.</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>470.4 = P * (1 + r/100)<sup>2</sup>...(1)</p><p>And</p><p>499.8 = P * (1 + /100)<sup>3</sup>...(2)</p><p>From equation (1) and (2),</p><p>470.4/499.8 = 1/(1 + r/100)</p><p>112/119 = 1/(1 + r/100)</p><p>112 + 112r/100 = 119</p><p>r = 700/112 = 6.25%</p><p>Now,</p><p>SI = 24000 * 6.25 * 4/100</p><p>SI = 240 * 25</p><p>SI = Rs.6000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A dishonest dealer professes to sell his goods at the cost price, but he uses a false weight of 820 grams per 1 kg weight. Find the percentage of his gain. (Correct up to two decimal places).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2312;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2357;&#2361; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 820 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;)&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["20.18%", "24.56%", "22.34%", "21.95%"], "options_hi": ["20.18%", "24.56%", "22.34%", "21.95%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Percentage gain = (True weight  -  False weight)/false weight * 100</p><p>True weight = 1000 grams</p><p>False weight = 820 grams</p><p>Percentage gain = (1000  -  820)/820 * 100 = 21.95%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Percentage gain = (True weight  -  False weight)/false weight * 100</p><p>True weight = 1000 grams</p><p>False weight = 820 grams</p><p>Percentage gain = (1000  -  820)/820 * 100 = 21.95%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the dimension of a cuboidal box is 6:4:5. If the diagonal of a cuboid is 2&radic;77cm then find the volume of the cuboidal box.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 6:4:5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; 2&radic;77cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["840cm<sup>3</sup>", "960cm<sup>3</sup>", "600cm<sup>3</sup>", "1210cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["840cm<sup>3</sup>", "960cm<sup>3</sup>", "600cm<sup>3</sup>", "1210cm<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the length, breadth and height of the cuboidal box are 6a, 4a and 5a respectively.</p><p>Diagonal of a cuboid = 2&radic;77cm</p><p>&radic;(l<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + h<sup>2</sup>) = 2&radic;77</p><p>(6a)<sup>2</sup> + (4a)<sup>2</sup> + (5a)<sup>2</sup> = 4*77 = 308</p><p>36a<sup>2</sup> + 16a<sup>2</sup> + 25a<sup>2</sup> = 308</p><p>77a<sup>2</sup> = 308</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> = 4</p><p>a = 2</p><p>So, the length, breadth and height of the cuboidal box are 12cm, 8cm and 10cm respectively.</p><p>Volume of the cuboidal box = 12*8*10 = 960cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the length, breadth and height of the cuboidal box are 6a, 4a and 5a respectively.</p><p>Diagonal of a cuboid = 2&radic;77cm</p><p>&radic;(l<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + h<sup>2</sup>) = 2&radic;77</p><p>(6a)<sup>2</sup> + (4a)<sup>2</sup> + (5a)<sup>2</sup> = 4*77 = 308</p><p>36a<sup>2</sup> + 16a<sup>2</sup> + 25a<sup>2</sup> = 308</p><p>77a<sup>2</sup> = 308</p><p>a<sup>2</sup> = 4</p><p>a = 2</p><p>So, the length, breadth and height of the cuboidal box are 12cm, 8cm and 10cm respectively.</p><p>Volume of the cuboidal box = 12*8*10 = 960cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of 3cot<sup>2</sup>60&deg;  -  8sin<sup>2</sup>30&deg; + sec<sup>2</sup>120&deg;.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>3cot<sup>2</sup>60&deg; - 8sin<sup>2</sup>30&deg; + sec<sup>2</sup>120&deg; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["5", "3", "4", "2"], "options_hi": ["5", "3", "4", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>3cot<sup>2</sup>60  -  8sin<sup>2</sup>30 + sec<sup>2</sup>120</p><p>= 3 * (1/&radic;3)<sup>2</sup>  -  8(1/2)<sup>2</sup> + sec<sup>2</sup>(90 + 30)</p><p>= 1  -  2 + (-cosec 30)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= -1 + 4</p><p>= 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>3cot<sup>2</sup>60  -  8sin<sup>2</sup>30 + sec<sup>2</sup>120</p><p>= 3 * (1/&radic;3)<sup>2</sup>  -  8(1/2)<sup>2</sup> + sec<sup>2</sup>(90 + 30)</p><p>= 1  -  2 + (-cosec 30)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= -1 + 4</p><p>= 3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a race around a circular track of 80 km, two cyclists are riding at a speed of 32 kmph and 16 kmph. After what time (in hours) will they meet at the point from where they started their journey?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>80 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325;&#2367;&#2354; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325; 32 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 16 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325;&#2367;&#2354; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["5", "8", "4", "9"], "options_hi": ["5", "8", "4", "9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Time taken by one cyclist = 80/32 hours</p><p>Time taken by other cyclist = 80/16 hours</p><p>Required time = LCM of (80/32) and (80/16)</p><p>= LCM of (5/2) and 5</p><p>= 5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Time taken by one cyclist = 80/32 hours</p><p>Time taken by other cyclist = 80/16 hours</p><p>Required time = LCM of (80/32) and (80/16)</p><p>= LCM of (5/2) and 5</p><p>= 5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The circumference of the two circles is 198 cm and 352 cm respectively. What is the difference between their radii?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 198 cm &#2324;&#2352; 352 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["45 cm", "16.5 cm", "49.5 cm", "24.5 cm"], "options_hi": ["45 cm", "16.5 cm", "49.5 cm", "24.5 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Circumference = 2&#960;r</p><p>Radius (r) = Circumference/2&#960;</p><p>Radius of circle having circumference 198 cm = 198/2&#960; = 31.5 cm</p><p>Radius of circle having circumference 352 cm = 352/2&#960; = 56 cm</p><p>Required difference = 56  -  31.5</p><p>= 24.5 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Circumference = 2&#960;r</p><p>Radius (r) = Circumference/2&#960;</p><p>Radius of circle having circumference 198 cm = 198/2&#960; = 31.5 cm</p><p>Radius of circle having circumference 352 cm = 352/2&#960; = 56 cm</p><p>Required difference = 56  -  31.5</p><p>= 24.5 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ten refrigerators and four mobile phones together cost &#8377; 2,10,000 while six refrigerators and two mobile phones together cost &#8377; 1,22,000. The cost (in &#8377;) of one refrigerator and two mobile phones is: </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2360; &#2352;&#2375;&#2347;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2379;&#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2347;&#2379;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377; 2,10,000 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2331;&#2361; &#2352;&#2375;&#2347;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2347;&#2379;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#8377; 1,22,000 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2347;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2347;&#2379;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["37000", "35200", "34500", "36000"], "options_hi": ["37000", "35200", "34500", "36000"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let cost of a refrigerator and a mobile is &#8377;R and &#8377;M respectively. </p><p>10R + 4M = 210000 ----(1)</p><p>6R + 2M = 122000 ----(2)</p><p>Eqn(1)  -  2*(eqn(2):</p><p>10R + 4M  -  2*(6R + 2M) = 210000  -  2*122000</p><p>2R = 34000</p><p>R = 17000</p><p>=&gt; 6*17000 + 2M = 122000</p><p>M = 10000</p><p>R + 2M = 17000 + 2*10000 = &#8377;37000 </p><p>Hence, cost of one refrigerator and two mobile phones = &#8377;37000 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let cost of a refrigerator and a mobile is &#8377;R and &#8377;M respectively. </p><p>10R + 4M = 210000 ----(1)</p><p>6R + 2M = 122000 ----(2)</p><p>Eqn(1)  -  2*(eqn(2):</p><p>10R + 4M  -  2*(6R + 2M) = 210000  -  2*122000</p><p>2R = 34000</p><p>R = 17000</p><p>=&gt; 6*17000 + 2M = 122000</p><p>M = 10000</p><p>R + 2M = 17000 + 2*10000 = &#8377;37000 </p><p>Hence, cost of one refrigerator and two mobile phones = &#8377;37000 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Vishal and Vinod started a busines with Rs.12000 and Rs.15000 respectively. After one year, Vishal withdrew p% of his capital while Vinod added Rs.3000 to his capital. If the profit received by Vishal and Vinod after 3 years partnership is in the ratio 8: 17 respectively, then find the value of p.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2342; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 12000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 15000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; p% &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2342; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 3000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2342; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8: 17 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; p &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["50", "45", "60", "25"], "options_hi": ["50", "45", "60", "25"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Amount invested by Vishal = Rs.12000</p><p>Amount invested by Vinod = Rs.15000</p><p>Then, profit ratio, Vishal: Vinod = (1 * 12000 + (3  -  1) * (100  -  p)% of 12000): (1 * 15000 + (3  -  1) * (15000 + 3000))</p><p>= (1200  -  8p): 1700</p><p>Also, profit ratio, Vishal: Vinod = 8: 17</p><p>Then, (1200  -  8p): 1700 = 8: 17</p><p><b>p = 50</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount invested by Vishal = Rs.12000</p><p>Amount invested by Vinod = Rs.15000</p><p>Then, profit ratio, Vishal: Vinod = (1 * 12000 + (3  -  1) * (100  -  p)% of 12000): (1 * 15000 + (3  -  1) * (15000 + 3000))</p><p>= (1200  -  8p): 1700</p><p>Also, profit ratio, Vishal: Vinod = 8: 17</p><p>Then, (1200  -  8p): 1700 = 8: 17</p><p><b>p = 50</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If a +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a + <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["3048190", "3048542", "3048132", "3048625"], "options_hi": ["3048190", "3048542", "3048132", "3048625"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Here,</p><p>(a+1/a)=7&radic;3</p><p>On Squaring both sides we get:</p><p>a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>+2=147</p><p>a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>=145</p><p>so:</p><p>we know by formula of (a+b)<sup>3</sup>=a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3</sup>+3ab(a+b)</p><p>(a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>)<sup>3</sup>=a<sup>6</sup>+1/a<sup>6</sup> +3(a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>(145)<sup>3</sup>= a<sup>6</sup>+1/a<sup>6</sup> +3*145</p><p>So, (a<sup>6</sup> + a<sup>-6</sup>)=3048190.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here,</p><p>(a+1/a)=7&radic;3</p><p>On Squaring both sides we get:</p><p>a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>+2=147</p><p>a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>=145</p><p>so:</p><p>we know by formula of (a+b)<sup>3</sup>=a<sup>3</sup>+b<sup>3</sup>+3ab(a+b)</p><p>(a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>)<sup>3</sup>=a<sup>6</sup>+1/a<sup>6</sup> +3(a<sup>2</sup>+1/a<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>(145)<sup>3</sup>= a<sup>6</sup>+1/a<sup>6</sup> +3*145</p><p>So, (a<sup>6</sup> + a<sup>-6</sup>)=3048190.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following quadratic equation has equal roots?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2328;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["4x<sup>2</sup>  -  6x + 2 = 0", "4x<sup>2</sup> + 20x + 16 = 0", "9x<sup>2</sup>  -  6x + 1 = 0", "None of these"], "options_hi": ["4x<sup>2</sup> - 6x + 2 = 0", "4x<sup>2</sup> + 20x + 16 = 0", "9x<sup>2</sup> - 6x + 1 = 0", "&#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>From (a): 4x<sup>2</sup>  -  6x + 2 = 0</p><p>4x<sup>2</sup>  -  4x  -  2x + 2 = 0</p><p>(4x  -  2)(x  -  1) = 0</p><p>x = 1/2, 1</p><p>From (b): 4x<sup>2</sup> + 20x + 16 = 0</p><p>4x<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 16x + 16 = 0</p><p>(4x + 16)(x + 1) = 0</p><p>x = -4, -1</p><p>From (c): 9x<sup>2</sup>  -  6x + 1 = 0</p><p>9x<sup>2</sup>  - 3x  -  3x + 1 = 0</p><p>(3x  -  1)(3x  -  1) = 0</p><p><b>x = 1/3, 1/3 (equal roots)</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From (a): 4x<sup>2</sup>  -  6x + 2 = 0</p><p>4x<sup>2</sup>  -  4x  -  2x + 2 = 0</p><p>(4x  -  2)(x  -  1) = 0</p><p>x = 1/2, 1</p><p>From (b): 4x<sup>2</sup> + 20x + 16 = 0</p><p>4x<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 16x + 16 = 0</p><p>(4x + 16)(x + 1) = 0</p><p>x = -4, -1</p><p>From (c): 9x<sup>2</sup>  -  6x + 1 = 0</p><p>9x<sup>2</sup>  - 3x  -  3x + 1 = 0</p><p>(3x  -  1)(3x  -  1) = 0</p><p><b>x = 1/3, 1/3 (equal roots)</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Madhu bought an article for Rs. X. The percentage of profit and loss after selling the article for Rs. 2645 and Rs. 1955 respectively is same. The value of X is :</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2343;&#2369; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2352;&#2369;. X &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2404; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2352;&#2369;. 2645 &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;. 1955 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376; :</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 2450", "Rs. 2400", "Rs. 2250", "Rs. 2300"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 2450", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2400", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2250", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2300"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let </p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2645  -  X)/X * 100 = (X  -  1955)/X * 100</p><p>2645  -  X = X  -  1955</p><p>2X = 4600</p><p>X = Rs. 2300</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let </p><p>According to question,</p><p>(2645  -  X)/X * 100 = (X  -  1955)/X * 100</p><p>2645  -  X = X  -  1955</p><p>2X = 4600</p><p>X = Rs. 2300</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Mr. Pankaj invested a certain amount at 8% per annum at simple interest. If the difference between the simple interest for 5 years and 6 years is Rs. 320, then what is the principal amount invested by Mr. Pankaj?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2306;&#2325;&#2332; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 8% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;. 320 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2306;&#2325;&#2332; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 3600", "Rs. 2000", "Rs. 6500", "Rs. 4000"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 3600", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2000", "&#2352;&#2369;. 6500", "&#2352;&#2369;. 4000"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let Rs. P be the principal amount of money.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(P * 8 * 6)/100  -  (P * 8 * 5)/100 = 320</p><p>=&gt; 0.08P = 320</p><p>=&gt; P = 320/0.08</p><p>=&gt; P = Rs. 4000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Rs. P be the principal amount of money.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(P * 8 * 6)/100  -  (P * 8 * 5)/100 = 320</p><p>=&gt; 0.08P = 320</p><p>=&gt; P = 320/0.08</p><p>=&gt; P = Rs. 4000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The number of elements only belongs to set A is 22, and number of elements only belongs to set B is 14. If A<img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15299/image029.png\">B = 3, then the number of elements in set B is what percent less than the number of elements in set A?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375;&#2335; A &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 22 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375;&#2335; B &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 14 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A<img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15299/image029.png\">B = 3, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2375;&#2335; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375;&#2335; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["24%", "30%", "28%", "32%"], "options_hi": ["24%", "30%", "28%", "32%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Number of elements only belongs to set A = 22</p><p>Number of elements only belongs to set B =14</p><p>Given,</p><p>A<img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15299/image029.png\">B = 3</p><p>So, number of elements in set A = 22 + 3 = 25</p><p>And number of elements in set B = 14 + 3 = 17</p><p>Required percentage = (8/25) * 100 = 32%.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of elements only belongs to set A = 22</p><p>Number of elements only belongs to set B =14</p><p>Given,</p><p>A<img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15299/image029.png\">B = 3</p><p>So, number of elements in set A = 22 + 3 = 25</p><p>And number of elements in set B = 14 + 3 = 17</p><p>Required percentage = (8/25) * 100 = 32%.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Express 0.32<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">64", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["816/2475", "812/2475", "808/2475", "820/2475"], "options_hi": ["0.002", "0.05", "0.005", "0.02"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=51 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image003.png\"></p><p>= (3264  -  32)/9900</p><p>= 808/2475</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=51 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image003.png\"></p><p>= (3264  -  32)/9900</p><p>= 808/2475</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}]}